## Auth

`POST {{.Prefix}}/auth/signup` (`email`, `password` 6 to 72 characters, `username` 3 to 30 characters) returns 201.
`POST {{.Prefix}}/auth/login` (`email`, `password`) returns 200 with `access_token` and `refresh_token`.

| Status | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| 400 | invalid body, or the password was rejected by the Supabase password policy |
| 401 | login: wrong email or password |
| 403 | login: email not confirmed yet |
| 409 | signup: an account with this email already exists |
| 429 | Supabase rate limit reached |
| 503 | the server was started without a database |
| 502 | Supabase failed for another reason (see the server log) |

Users live in Supabase Auth (`auth.users`); the app never stores passwords. Set `SUPABASE_KEY` to the **anon (public) key**, never the `service_role` key. In the Supabase dashboard, *Confirm email* decides whether login returns 403 until the user confirms.

The username is sent as user metadata (`raw_user_meta_data->>'username'`). `GET {{.Prefix}}/test/db` queries a `user_profile` table, which is optional for signup and login. Example to run in the Supabase SQL editor:

```sql
create table public.user_profile (
  user_id  uuid primary key references auth.users (id) on delete cascade,
  username text not null,
  constraint username_format check (username ~ '^[A-Za-z0-9_.-]{3,30}$')
);

alter table public.user_profile enable row level security;

create function public.handle_new_user() returns trigger
language plpgsql security definer set search_path = public as $$
begin
  insert into public.user_profile (user_id, username)
  values (new.id, new.raw_user_meta_data ->> 'username');
  return new;
end;
$$;

create trigger on_auth_user_created
  after insert on auth.users
  for each row execute function public.handle_new_user();
```
{{- end}}

## Layout

| Path | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `main.go` | loads `.env`, starts the server |
| `http/` | Gin engine + CORS (`ALLOWED_ORIGINS`) |
| `routes/routes.register.go` | parent group `{{.Prefix}}`, registers the routes |
| `routes/ping/` | the placeholder route |
{{- if .DB}}
| `database/database.client.interface.go` | `IDatabase` interface, `AuthSession` and the `Err*` auth errors |
| `database/supabase/supabase.go` | Supabase implementation (queries and auth) |
| `database/supabase/errors.go` | maps Supabase Auth errors to the `Err*` values |
| `routes/signup/`, `routes/login/` | auth routes |
{{- end}}
{{- if .Payment}}
| `paymentprocessor/interface.payment.processor.go` | `IPaymentProcessor` interface |
| `paymentprocessor/{{.Payment}}/` | {{.Payment}} implementation (needs `STRIPE_TEST_KEY`) |
| `routes/payments/` | payment route |
{{- end}}
| `service/` | services used by the routes |

## Adding a route

1. Add `service/<name>.go` and a field on `service.Services`.
2. Add `routes/<name>/<name>.go` with a `Register...Routes(rg, svc)` function.
3. Register it in `routes/routes.register.go`.
